###
# Cross-cutting error handling (Problem Details). These don't depend on any resource
# created above - every response here should carry a "correlationId" extension and a
# "type": "https://httpstatuses.io/{status}" (or urn:ordinis:error:... for DomainException).

### Malformed JSON body - expect 400, routed through ProblemDetailsFactory (not ASP.NET Core's default shape)
POST {{Ordinis.Api_HostAddress}}/api/v1/organizations
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{not valid json

### Malformed enum value in body - expect 400
POST {{Ordinis.Api_HostAddress}}/api/v1/users
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "organizationId": "{{organizationId}}",
  "displayName": "Bad Enum User",
  "email": "bad-enum@example.com",
  "password": "SuperSecret123",
  "orgRole": "NotARole"
}

### Non-guid value in a :guid route segment - expect 404
GET {{Ordinis.Api_HostAddress}}/api/v1/tasks/not-a-guid

### Unmatched route - expect 404 with a Problem Details body (via UseStatusCodePages)
GET {{Ordinis.Api_HostAddress}}/api/v1/nonexistent

### Disallowed HTTP method on a real route - expect 405 with a Problem Details body
PATCH {{Ordinis.Api_HostAddress}}/api/v1/tasks

### Minimal API query parameter that fails to bind - expect 400, not 500
# (BadHttpRequestException is caught in its own clause in GlobalExceptionMiddleware,
# before the generic catch-all)
GET {{Ordinis.Api_HostAddress}}/api/v1/search?q=x&type=tasks&page=abc

### Get after delete - expect 404
GET {{Ordinis.Api_HostAddress}}/api/v1/projects/{{projectId}}

###
